  "pending": {
    "linkedin:a93107a62587d4dc708f2895": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Associate Software Developer (AI)",
        "company": "Precisely",
        "location": "Phoenix, AZ, USA",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487940890",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "2026-11-09T00:00:00+00:00",
        "is_remote": true,
        "description": "At Precisely, we're not just building software — we're shaping the future of data integrity. As a global leader in data quality, data enrichment, and location intelligence, Precisely helps thousands of the world's most trusted brands make confident decisions with data they can rely on. We're an AI-first organization, which means artificial intelligence isn't a buzzword here — it's woven into how we build products, how we work, and how we think about solving complex problems for our customers. When you join Precisely, you join a team of curious, driven innovators who believe that better data makes the world run better. If you're ready to do meaningful work at the intersection of AI and data — and help define what's possible — we'd love for you to apply!\nOverview\nWe are seeking a passionate Associate Software Developer (AI) to join our engineering team building scalable applications. This role is ideal for a candidate who is eager to learn, contribute, and grow in a collaborative, fast-paced environment. You will work under the guidance of experienced developers, participate in real projects, and build your skills with modern languages, frameworks, and practices.\nWhat You Will Do\nAssist in designing, developing, and maintaining AI-enabled applications using modern programming languages such as Python, TypeScript, Java, C#, or Go.\nWork with team members to understand requirements and implement features.\nLearn to use Pydantic for defining and validating data models.\nWrite clean, well-documented, object-oriented code with guidance.\nParticipate in code reviews and incorporate feedback.\nHelp troubleshoot and resolve basic technical issues.\nSupport testing and CI/CD processes.\nWhat We Are Looking For\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent experience.\nAt least 1 year of experience building enterprise-level software.\nSolid proficiency in at least one modern, general-purpose language, such as Python, TypeScript/JavaScript, Java, C#, or Go.\nWorking knowledge of object-oriented programming principles and design patterns.\nExperience building or consuming REST APIs.\nFamiliarity with popular frameworks and libraries in your language of choice, such as FastAPI, Django, Flask, Node.js/Express, NestJS, Spring Boot, .NET, or React.\nEagerness to learn new languages, frameworks, and tools as our stack evolves.\nStrong problem-solving and communication skills.\nWillingness to take initiative and accept feedback.\nAbility to work effectively in a team and follow instructions.\nAI Skills/Knowledge\nKnowledge of large language models (LLMs) and experience with AI coding assistants such as Claude Code or GitHub Copilot.\nPreferred Skills (a Plus But Not Required)\nExposure to web development (frontend and backend), including building and consuming APIs\nFamiliarity with Git and unit/integration testing\nExposure to data engineering concepts\nExposure to cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure), Docker, and CI/CD tooling\nThis position is 100% remote anywhere in the US\nApplication and Interview Impersonation Notice: Impersonating another individual when applying for employment, and/or participating in an interview process to assist another individual in obtaining employment, with Precisely Software Incorporated (“Precisely”) is unlawful. If Precisely identifies such fraudulent conduct, then as applicable and to the extent permitted by law, the application will be rejected, an offer (if made) will be rescinded, or the employment will be terminated, and legal action may be taken against the impersonators.\nThe personal data that you provide as a part of this job application will be handled in accordance with relevant laws. For more information about how Precisely handles the personal data of job applicants, please see the Precisely Candidate Privacy Notice",
