    "linkedin:e84f31da7c8fd898c1d7fb3b": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Frontend Engineer (React.Js, UX)",
        "company": "Superworq",
        "location": "USA",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489206473",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "2026-11-12T00:00:00+00:00",
        "is_remote": true,
        "description": "About The Company\nGN is a global leader in intelligent hearing, audio, video, and gaming solutions, dedicated to improving lives through technology that enhances the senses of hearing and sight. Founded in 1869, GN has a rich heritage of innovation and a commitment to bringing people closer through advanced sound solutions. The company’s broad portfolio includes medical-grade hearing technology brands such as ReSound, Beltone, Interton, and Jabra, as well as professional collaboration and gaming brands including Jabra, BlueParrott, FalCom, and SteelSeries. With a workforce of approximately 7,000 employees and a presence in around 100 countries, GN is publicly traded on Nasdaq Copenhagen (GN.CO). The company fosters a culture of community, openness, and understanding, driven by customer insights and expertise in wireless technologies, software, and miniaturization.\nAbout The Role\nWe are seeking a skilled Frontend Engineer to join our Growth Engineering team, contributing to the development of customer-facing web experiences for Jabra Enhance. This fully remote position based in the United States offers the opportunity to build and evolve seamless digital journeys that support users on their hearing journey. Reporting to the Senior Engineering Manager, Growth, you will own key web-based customer journeys from technical design through delivery. Collaborating closely with design and engineering colleagues, you will translate thoughtful UI/UX concepts into accessible, high-performing, and intuitive products. The role emphasizes practical problem-solving, continuous improvement, and a commitment to quality outcomes within an Agile environment.\nQualifications\nProven experience developing modern web applications using React.js and contemporary JavaScript libraries and tooling\nStrong understanding of HTML rendering, CSS, JavaScript, single-page applications, and both client-side and server-side rendering\nExperience with server-side technologies such as Node.js is a plus\nDemonstrated attention to design, usability, and delivering an exceptional customer experience\nBackground as a Frontend or Full Stack Engineer with collaborative teamwork skills\nExperience with Shopify technologies including Liquid, Storefront/Admin APIs, theme or app development is preferred but not required\nAbility to participate effectively in Agile ceremonies and collaborate during East Coast business hours\nResponsibilities\nDevelop and enhance customer-facing features and end-to-end web journeys using React.js, JavaScript, CSS, Relay, and GraphQL\nPlan, architect, build, and maintain core external-facing web applications\nPartner with design teams to translate UI/UX concepts into accessible, intuitive, and technically feasible experiences\nCreate reusable components, code, and libraries to support scalable product development\nImprove application performance, reliability, and efficiency through debugging, profiling, and optimization\nParticipate in code refactoring and architecture reviews to ensure maintainable, high-quality solutions\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams and contribute to Agile development processes\nBenefits\nCompetitive salary range from $135,000 to $150,000 annually, with discretionary bonuses\nFully remote work opportunity within the United States\nCollaborative and inclusive work environment focused on continuous improvement\nOpportunity to work on innovative products that positively impact people’s lives\nAccess to professional growth within a leading global technology company\nCommitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in the workplace\nReasonable accommodations available for applicants with disabilities\nEqual Opportunity\nGN is an Equal Opportunity Employer that values a diverse and inclusive workforce. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, age, gender identity, sexual orientation, marital status, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other basis prohibited by federal, state, or local law. Women, minorities, veterans, LGBTQIA+ individuals, and persons with disabilities are strongly encouraged to apply. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations for applicants with disabilities during the recruitment process.",
