    "linkedin:ec12b3d3e6c0589b9b366fc3": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Junior Software Developer",
        "company": "Salute Medical Transportation",
        "location": "San Antonio, TX, USA",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4490373134",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "2026-11-12T00:00:00+00:00",
        "is_remote": true,
        "description": "Location Requirement: Texas (remote - BYOD)\nPosition is fully remote, only applicants in Texas considered .\nAll applicants must be eligible to work in the U.S. We do not offer sponsorship visas and will not consider applicants located outside the U.S.\nPositions Available : 2 (1 - front-end focused, 1 - back-end focused)\nResponsibilities\nPosition would be to join a small web application development project. New employee will join a small team (2 developers) in the development of a web-based transportation management solution. The application being developed will help route drivers and schedule their work days as well as perform other administrative functions. The end goal will be to develop a dispatch and routing platform it will communicate with the native app (similar to Uber driver's app) and provide administrative personnel up to date information regarding trip status.\nRequired Skills:\nExcellent communication skills\nBasic to intermediate experience with JavaScript, particularly server-side development with Node.js.\nExperience working with SQL databases, including writing basic to intermediate SQL queries, SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, joins, and filtering.\nAbility to understand and adjust CSS code\nFamiliarity with EJS or other server-side templating technologies.\nUnderstanding of JSON and how it is used to exchange data between applications and APIs.\nBasic understanding of REST APIs and HTTP methods such as GET, POST, PUT, and DELETE.\nExperience working with or willingness to learn PowerShell for scripting, automation, and interaction with the application environment.\nUnderstanding of fundamental programming concepts such as variables, functions, loops, conditional statements, arrays, objects, and error handling.\nAbility to troubleshoot problems by reading error messages, reviewing logs, and debugging code.\nBasic understanding of web application architecture, including the relationship between the front end, back end, database, and APIs.\nAbility to work with existing code and understand, modify, and extend functionality without unnecessarily rewriting existing systems.\nFamiliarity with Git or another source-control system.\nStrong attention to detail and willingness to thoroughly test changes before deploying them.\nMust be able to work independently on assigned tasks\nNice Have Skills\nExperience with Node.js and Express.js.\nExperience with CSS\nExperience developing or maintaining SQL Server/Microsoft SQL Server databases.\nExperience creating and consuming REST APIs.\nFamiliarity with asynchronous JavaScript, including Promises and async/await.\nExperience working with database queries from a Node.js application.\nFamiliarity with PowerShell scripting and Windows environments.\nExperience troubleshooting production or business-critical applications.\nFamiliarity with authentication, authorization, and basic web application security practices.\nExperience working with JSON-based API requests and responses.\nExposure to deployment, server administration, or application configuration.\nUI/UX experience if applying for front-end role. Experienced designers considered if back-end is not a strong suit.\nSalary Range : $50,000-$70,000 (based on experience)\nWe are looking for a junior software developer to join our existing team. This role is fully remote and strong preference is given to applicants in Texas. Annual on-sites are required in San Antonio, TX so willingness to travel is required.\nApplication Process\nLooking to fill the role immediately. Due to bots/spam hitting application caps quickly please submit your application to the below form. Only applicants on the form will be manually reviewed: https://forms.gle/XBQHxeexbY1Dnfie7\nThe application process should take less than a month: short zoom interview to discuss basic qualifications and expectations for the role. After this interview a longer technical interview with the senior developer on the project will be scheduled.",
